Isis claims responsibility for the  murder of four Western tourists  including an American couple in  Tajikistan Jay Austin and Morgan Loren  giggin from Washington DC died in the  car and knife attack  chip Reid looks at the two Americans who  were far from home on their bicycles  Shep good morning  well good morning a little more than a  year ago Jay Austin and Lauren Gagan  both just 29 years old quit their  comfortable office jobs in Washington  and set out for an adventure traveling  the world by bicycle sadly their ride  ended in tragedy in the mountains of  Tajikistan Jay Austin and Lauren Gagan  chronicled their adventures on their  website simply cycling as they pedaled  their way through Africa Europe and  Central Asia Austin wrote they chose to  see the world by bike because life is  short and the world is big and we want  to make the most out of our youth and  good health before they're gone they  were both just the kind of people that  you wanted to open your heart to Molly  Scalise was gegen friend and roommate  they were the most kind empathetic  principles people that I knew the  couple's dream ended suddenly Sunday in  Tajikistan near the border with  Afghanistan when terrorists ran into  their group with a car and then attacked  them with knives they were killed along  with two Europeans and three other  Europeans were injured Taji Cathar DS  say police tracked down five of the isis  suspects killing four of them on their  blog austin had written of the  challenges of their trip writing bikes  create the expectation that disaster is  pretty much inevitable and should be  embraced but he also wrote it was a  privilege to see some amazing places  meet some wonderful people and spend  lots and lots of time with a really  lovely girl they were such an example of  a intentional life and a principled life  and had so much love to give and i'm  glad that they had the opportunity to to  bring that to so many people around the  world the State Department has offered  assistance but the investigation is  being led by Tajikistan's mother told us  over the phone her son was a gentle soul  who simply wanted to leave the world a  better place  Anthony chip Reed thank you chip
 

